{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat rehearsal/{README.md,run.mjs,workspace.mjs,agent.mjs,audit.mjs,summary.mjs,files.mjs}'","aggregated_output":"# DX12 agent rehearsal\n\nRun from the repository root with an authenticated Codex CLI or Claude Code installation, the existing development dependencies, system Chrome, and the built documentation and packed Axylo tarball.\n\n```sh\nnode rehearsal/run.mjs --agent codex --model YOUR_MODEL_ID --effort high --task daily-visits --workdir /tmp/axylo-runs\nnode rehearsal/summary.mjs\n```\n\nUse `--agent claude` for Claude Code. The runner applies `--effort` to Codex. Claude's stream reports the model and leaves the observed effort empty. The task IDs are `daily-visits`, `regional-sales`, `signups`, and `daily-revenue`. The runner uses the system temporary directory if `--workdir` is omitted and creates a fresh subdirectory for each run. The agent has 20 minutes by default. To override that limit, pass `--timeout-ms` in milliseconds.\n\nThe workspace draws from `apps/docs/dist` and `tests/dist/.packed/axylo-0.0.0.tgz`. The docs include their published examples and omit the internal repository snapshots linked from conformance evidence. The fixture and fixed prompt are the other inputs. The grader supplies the original fixture to `render`, so changes to an agent's scratch copy of `data.json` cannot change the data being graded.\n\nThe runner keeps each run under `rehearsal/records/` with the transcript, stderr, delivered chart if present, grade, and run metadata. The transcript audit checks recorded command lines and tool inputs for paths outside the workspace, with exceptions for system executables and `/dev/null`. It reports detected paths and any malformed transcript lines. It can only check accesses visible in the transcript and paths it can resolve. A void run remains in the summary with its grade for inspection. These records are agent rehearsal only.\n\nTo regrade a prepared workspace, use the workspace path printed by the runner.\n\n```sh\nnode rehearsal/grade.mjs --task daily-visits --workdir /path/to/run/workspace\n```\n\nThe grader uses two headless Chrome contexts with English (US) formatting and different time zones. The expected JSON gives table rows in reading order. An expected `null` is a missing observation. The table may omit a wholly missing row or label it “No data.” Chart types are read from Axylo's accessible plot description or generated summary. The grader opens the standard “View as table” control.\n\nThe runner and standalone grader return 0 for a pass, 1 for a failed grade or void run, and 2 for a setup or tool error.\n\n```sh\nnpx --no-install vitest run --root rehearsal\nnpx --no-install vitest run --root rehearsal --exclude '**/*.browser.test.mjs'\n```\n\nThe first command includes the Chrome tests. The second checks the fixtures, audit, agent invocation, workspace setup, and pre-browser grading without opening Chrome.\nimport { copyFile, lstat, mkdir, readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { parseArgs } from 'node:util';\nimport { observeAgent, runAgent } from './agent.mjs';\nimport { auditTranscript } from './audit.mjs';\nimport { isMain, rehearsal, writeJson } from './files.mjs';\nimport { grade } from './grade.mjs';\nimport { prepareWorkspace } from './workspace.mjs';\n\nasync function reserveRecord(date, agent, task) {\n  const records = join(rehearsal, 'records');\n  await mkdir(records, { recursive: true });\n  for (let n = 1; ; n++) {\n    const record = join(records, `${date}-${agent}-${task}-${n}`);\n    try {\n      await mkdir(record);\n      return record;\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (error.code !== 'EEXIST') throw error;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nasync function main() {\n  const { values } = parseArgs({\n    options: {\n      agent: { type: 'string' }, model: { type: 'string' }, effort: { type: 'string' }, task: { type: 'string' },\n      workdir: { type: 'string', default: tmpdir() }, 'timeout-ms': { type: 'string', default: '1200000' },\n    },\n  });\n  const { agent, model, effort, task, workdir } = values;\n  const timeoutMs = Number(values['timeout-ms']);\n  if (!['codex', 'claude'].includes(agent) || !model || !task ||\n      !Number.isSafeInteger(timeoutMs) || timeoutMs < 1 || timeoutMs > 2147483647) {\n    throw new Error('Usage: node rehearsal/run.mjs --agent codex|claude --model <id> [--effort <e>] --task <id> [--workdir <dir>] [--timeout-ms <ms>]');\n  }\n\n  const { workspace, runDirectory } = await prepareWorkspace(workdir, task);\n  console.log('Workspace: ' + workspace);\n  const start = new Date();\n  const { transcript, stderr, exit } = await runAgent(agent, { model, effort, workspace, runDirectory, timeoutMs });\n  const end = new Date();\n  const log = await readFile(transcript, 'utf8');\n  const [audit, observed] = await Promise.all([auditTranscript(log, workspace), observeAgent(agent, log)]);\n  const record = await reserveRecord(start.toISOString().slice(0, 10), agent, task);\n  await copyFile(transcript, join(record, 'transcript.jsonl'));\n  await copyFile(stderr, join(record, 'stderr.log'));\n\n  const answer = join(workspace, 'chart.js');\n  const answerStat = await lstat(answer).catch(error => {\n    if (error.code !== 'ENOENT') throw error;\n  });\n  if (answerStat?.isFile()) await copyFile(answer, join(record, 'chart.js'));\n  let result;\n  try {\n    result = await grade(workspace, task);\n  } catch (error) {\n    result = { pass: false, criteria: [{ name: 'grader', pass: false, detail: String(error) }], diagnostics: [], timezones: [] };\n    await writeJson(join(workspace, 'grade.json'), result);\n  }\n  await copyFile(join(workspace, 'grade.json'), join(record, 'grade.json'));\n  await writeJson(join(record, 'run.json'), {\n    kind: 'agent rehearsal', agent, task, requested: { model, effort: effort ?? null }, observed,\n    startedAt: start.toISOString(), endedAt: end.toISOString(), durationMs: end - start,\n    timeoutMs, exit, ...audit,\n  });\n  const agentFailed = exit.code !== 0 || exit.timedOut || exit.error !== null;\n  const status = audit.void ? 'void' : agentFailed || !result.pass ? 'fail' : 'pass';\n  console.log(`Agent rehearsal: ${status}. Record: ${record}`);\n  process.exitCode = exit.error || result.criteria.some(item => ['browser', 'grader'].includes(item.name)) ? 2\n    : status === 'pass' ? 0 : 1;\n}\n\nif (isMain(import.meta.url)) {\n  try {\n    await main();\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(String(error));\n    process.exitCode = 2;\n  }\n}\nimport { execFile } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { copyFile, cp, mkdir, mkdtemp, realpath, stat, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { join, relative, resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { promisify } from 'node:util';\nimport { inside, repository, taskFiles } from './files.mjs';\n\nexport async function prepareWorkspace(directory, task) {\n  const { prompt, fixture, expected } = taskFiles(task);\n  await stat(expected);\n\n  const scratch = resolve(directory);\n  const repo = await realpath(repository);\n  // Check the nearest existing ancestor before creating any directories through a symlink.\n  let ancestor = scratch;\n  while (true) {\n    try {\n      if (inside(repo, await realpath(ancestor))) throw new Error('--workdir must be outside the repository.');\n      break;\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (error.code !== 'ENOENT') throw error;\n      ancestor = resolve(ancestor, '..');\n    }\n  }\n  await mkdir(scratch, { recursive: true });\n  const runDirectory = await mkdtemp(join(await realpath(scratch), 'axylo-rehearsal-'));\n  const workspace = join(runDirectory, 'workspace');\n  const docs = join(repository, 'apps/docs/dist');\n  const tarball = join(repository, 'tests/dist/.packed/axylo-0.0.0.tgz');\n  const installed = join(workspace, 'node_modules/axylo');\n  await mkdir(installed, { recursive: true });\n  await cp(docs, join(workspace, 'docs'), {\n    recursive: true,\n    filter(file) {\n      const path = relative(docs, file);\n      // Linked public examples belong to the docs. The evidence pages also link to internal source snapshots.\n      return !path.startsWith('source/') || path === 'source/apps' || path === 'source/apps/docs' ||\n        /^source\\/(?:apps\\/docs\\/)?examples(?:\\/|$)/.test(path);\n    },\n  });\n  await promisify(execFile)('tar', ['-xzf', tarball, '--strip-components=1', '-C', installed]);\n  await copyFile(fixture, join(workspace, 'data.json'));\n  await copyFile(prompt, join(workspace, 'PROMPT.md'));\n  await writeFile(join(workspace, 'package.json'), '{\"type\":\"module\"}\\n');\n  return { workspace, runDirectory };\n}\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { open, readdir, readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { transcriptEvents } from './audit.mjs';\n\nconst claudeTools = 'Read,Write,Edit,Glob,Grep,Bash(node:*),Bash(ls:*),Bash(cat:*)';\n\nexport function agentArgs(agent, { model, effort, workspace }) {\n  if (agent === 'codex') {\n    return ['exec', '-m', model, ...(effort ? ['-c', 'model_reasoning_effort=' + JSON.stringify(effort)] : []),\n      '-s', 'workspace-write', '--skip-git-repo-check', '-C', workspace, '--json', '-'];\n  }\n  return ['-p', '--model', model, '--output-format', 'stream-json', '--verbose', '--allowedTools', claudeTools];\n}\n\nexport async function runAgent(agent, options) {\n  const { workspace, runDirectory, timeoutMs } = options;\n  const transcript = join(runDirectory, 'transcript.jsonl');\n  const stderr = join(runDirectory, 'stderr.log');\n  const handles = [];\n  let exit;\n  try {\n    for (const [name, flags] of [[join(workspace, 'PROMPT.md'), 'r'], [transcript, 'wx'], [stderr, 'wx']]) {\n      handles.push(await open(name, flags));\n    }\n    exit = await new Promise(resolve => {\n      const grouped = process.platform !== 'win32';\n      const child = spawn(agent, agentArgs(agent, options), {\n        cwd: workspace,\n        stdio: handles.map(handle => handle.fd),\n        detached: grouped,\n      });\n      let timedOut = false;\n      let spawnError = null;\n      let force;\n      const stop = signal => {\n        if (!child.pid) return;\n        try {\n          if (grouped) process.kill(-child.pid, signal);\n          else child.kill(signal);\n        } catch (error) {\n          if (error.code !== 'ESRCH') spawnError ??= String(error);\n        }\n      };\n      const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n        timedOut = true;\n        stop('SIGTERM');\n        force = setTimeout(() => stop('SIGKILL'), 2000);\n      }, timeoutMs);\n      child.on('error', error => { spawnError = String(error); });\n      child.on('close', (code, signal) => {\n        clearTimeout(timer);\n        clearTimeout(force);\n        if (timedOut) stop('SIGKILL');\n        resolve({ code, signal, timedOut, error: spawnError });\n      });\n    });\n  } finally {\n    await Promise.all(handles.map(handle => handle.close()));\n  }\n  return { transcript, stderr, exit };\n}\n\nexport async function observeAgent(agent, transcript, sessions = join(process.env.CODEX_HOME || join(homedir(), '.codex'), 'sessions')) {\n  const { events } = transcriptEvents(transcript);\n  const observed = { model: null, effort: null };\n  if (agent === 'claude') {\n    const models = events.filter(event => event.type === 'assistant').map(event => event.message?.model)\n      .filter(model => typeof model === 'string');\n    return { ...observed, model: models.at(-1) ?? null };\n  }\n\n  const threadId = events[0]?.type === 'thread.started' ? events[0].thread_id : null;\n  if (!threadId || !/^[\\w-]+$/.test(threadId)) return observed;\n  observed.threadId = threadId;\n  try {\n    const entries = await readdir(sessions, { recursive: true, withFileTypes: true });\n    const rollout = entries.find(entry => entry.isFile() && entry.name.startsWith('rollout-') &&\n      entry.name.endsWith('-' + threadId + '.jsonl'));\n    if (!rollout) return { ...observed, detail: 'No rollout found for this Codex thread.' };\n    const { events: session } = transcriptEvents(await readFile(join(rollout.parentPath, rollout.name), 'utf8'));\n    const turn = session.findLast(event => event.type === 'turn_context')?.payload;\n    observed.model = turn?.model ?? null;\n    observed.effort = turn?.effort ?? turn?.reasoning_effort ?? turn?.model_reasoning_effort ?? null;\n    if (!turn) observed.detail = 'No turn_context found in the Codex rollout.';\n  } catch (error) {\n    observed.detail = 'Could not read Codex rollout metadata: ' + (error.code ?? error.message);\n  }\n  return observed;\n}\nimport { constants } from 'node:fs';\nimport { access, realpath } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\nimport { dirname, resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport { inside } from './files.mjs';\n\nexport function transcriptEvents(transcript) {\n  const events = [];\n  let malformedLines = 0;\n  for (const line of transcript.split('\\n')) {\n    if (!line.trim()) continue;\n    try {\n      const event = JSON.parse(line);\n      if (event && typeof event === 'object') events.push(event);\n      else malformedLines++;\n    } catch {\n      malformedLines++;\n    }\n  }\n  return { events, malformedLines };\n}\n\nfunction * toolInputs(event) {\n  const item = event.item;\n  if (item?.type === 'command_execution') yield { command: item.command, cwd: item.cwd ?? item.workdir };\n  if (item?.type === 'file_change') yield { changes: item.changes };\n  if (item?.type === 'mcp_tool_call') yield item.arguments ?? item.input;\n  if (event.type === 'tool_use') yield event.input;\n  if (event.type === 'assistant') {\n    for (const part of event.message?.content ?? []) {\n      if (part.type === 'tool_use') yield part.input;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction * unquotedPaths(command) {\n  const paths = /(?<![\\w./:-])(?:file:\\/\\/\\/|~\\/|\\$(?:HOME|\\{HOME\\})\\/|\\.\\.?\\/|\\/)[^\\s\"'\\x60;&|<>()[\\]{}*,]*|(?<!\\S)(?:~|\\$(?:HOME|\\{HOME\\}))(?=$|[\\s;&|])/g;\n  for (const match of command.matchAll(paths)) yield match[0];\n  for (const match of command.matchAll(/(?<![\\w./:-])[\\w.-]+(?:\\/[\\w.-]+)*(?![\\w./:-])/g)) yield match[0];\n}\n\nfunction * commandPaths(command) {\n  if (typeof command !== 'string') return;\n  let offset = 0;\n  // Keep spaces in literal paths, and inspect commands quoted for a shell or Node's -e.\n  for (const match of command.matchAll(/\"([^\"\\n]+)\"|'([^'\\n]+)'/g)) {\n    yield * unquotedPaths(command.slice(offset, match.index));\n    const quoted = match[1] ?? match[2];\n    if (/^(?:file:\\/\\/|[~/]|\\.\\.?\\/)[^;&|<>()[\\]{}\"'\\n]*$/.test(quoted) && !/\\s[-/]/.test(quoted)) {\n      yield quoted;\n    } else {\n      yield * commandPaths(quoted);\n    }\n    offset = match.index + match[0].length;\n  }\n  yield * unquotedPaths(command.slice(offset));\n}\n\nfunction localPath(text, base) {\n  if (text.startsWith('file://')) {\n    try { return fileURLToPath(text); } catch { return undefined; }\n  }\n  if (/^[\\w+.-]+:\\/\\//.test(text)) return undefined;\n  return resolve(base, text.replace(/^(?:~|\\$HOME|\\$\\{HOME\\})(?=\\/|$)/, homedir()));\n}\n\nasync function resolveLinks(file) {\n  try {\n    return await realpath(file);\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error.code !== 'ENOENT' && error.code !== 'ENOTDIR') throw error;\n    const parent = dirname(file);\n    return parent === file ? file : resolve(await resolveLinks(parent), file.slice(parent === '/' ? 1 : parent.length + 1));\n  }\n}\n\nasync function systemTool(file) {\n  if (file === '/dev/null') return true;\n  if (!/^\\/(?:usr\\/(?:local\\/)?)?(?:bin|sbin)\\/[^/]+$/.test(file)) return false;\n  try {\n    await access(file, constants.X_OK);\n    return true;\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\nconst pathKeys = /^(?:(?:file|target|source|destination|absolute|relative)[_-]?)?(?:path|paths|file|files|uri|uris)$|^(?:dir|directory|cwd|workdir|working_directory)$/i;\nconst commandKeys = /^(?:cmd|command|command_line|argv)$/i;\n\nexport async function auditTranscript(transcript, workspace) {\n  workspace = await realpath(workspace);\n  const paths = new Set();\n  const checked = new Set();\n  const { events, malformedLines } = transcriptEvents(transcript);\n\n  async function check(text, base) {\n    if (!text || text === '-') return;\n    const path = localPath(text, base);\n    if (!path || checked.has(path)) return;\n    checked.add(path);\n    if (await systemTool(path)) return;\n    if (!inside(workspace, path)) {\n      paths.add(path);\n      return;\n    }\n    const actual = await resolveLinks(path);\n    if (!inside(workspace, actual) && !await systemTool(actual)) paths.add(actual);\n  }\n\n  async function scan(value, base, key = '') {\n    if (typeof value === 'string') {\n      if (commandKeys.test(key)) {\n        for (const path of commandPaths(value)) await check(path, base);\n      } else if (pathKeys.test(key)) {\n        await check(value, base);\n      } else if (key === 'arguments') {\n        try { value = JSON.parse(value); } catch { return; }\n        await scan(value, base);\n      }\n      return;\n    }\n    if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n      for (const part of value) await scan(part, base, key);\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return;\n    const cwd = value.cwd ?? value.workdir ?? value.working_directory;\n    if (typeof cwd === 'string') await check(cwd, base);\n    const directory = typeof cwd === 'string' ? localPath(cwd, base) ?? base : base;\n    // One recorded external working directory is enough, without treating every shell word as a path there.\n    if (!inside(workspace, directory)) return;\n    for (const [name, part] of Object.entries(value)) {\n      if (part !== cwd || (name !== 'cwd' && name !== 'workdir' && name !== 'working_directory')) {\n        await scan(part, directory, name);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (const event of events) {\n    for (const input of toolInputs(event)) {\n      if (typeof input === 'string') await scan(input, workspace, 'arguments');\n      else await scan(input, workspace);\n    }\n  }\n  return { void: paths.size > 0, paths: [...paths].sort(), malformedLines };\n}\nimport { readdir } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { readJson, rehearsal } from './files.mjs';\n\nconst root = join(rehearsal, 'records');\nconst entries = await readdir(root, { withFileTypes: true }).catch(error => {\n  if (error.code === 'ENOENT') return [];\n  throw error;\n});\nconst rows = [];\nfor (const entry of entries.filter(entry => entry.isDirectory()).sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))) {\n  const directory = join(root, entry.name);\n  try {\n    const run = await readJson(join(directory, 'run.json'));\n    const grade = await readJson(join(directory, 'grade.json'));\n    const agentFailed = run.exit.code !== 0 || run.exit.timedOut || run.exit.error !== null;\n    const failed = grade.criteria.filter(item => !item.pass).map(item => item.name);\n    if (agentFailed) failed.unshift(run.exit.timedOut ? 'agent timeout' : 'agent exit');\n    if (run.void) failed.unshift('outside workspace');\n    rows.push([\n      entry.name, run.agent, run.observed.model ?? `${run.requested.model} (requested)`, run.task,\n      run.void ? 'void' : grade.pass && !agentFailed ? 'yes' : 'no', failed.join(', ') || '—',\n    ]);\n  } catch (error) {\n    rows.push([entry.name, '—', '—', '—', 'incomplete', String(error)]);\n  }\n}\n\nconsole.log('DX12 agent rehearsal');\nconst headings = ['Record', 'Agent', 'Model', 'Task', 'Pass', 'Failed criteria'];\nconst widths = headings.map((heading, i) => Math.max(heading.length, ...rows.map(row => row[i].length)));\nfor (const row of [headings, ...rows]) {\n  console.log(row.map((value, i) => value.padEnd(widths[i])).join('  ').trimEnd());\n}\nimport { readFile, rename, rm, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { randomUUID } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { isAbsolute, join, relative, sep } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\n\nexport const rehearsal = fileURLToPath(new URL('.', import.meta.url));\nexport const repository = fileURLToPath(new URL('..', import.meta.url));\n\nexport function inside(root, file) {\n  const path = relative(root, file);\n  return path !== '..' && !path.startsWith('..' + sep) && !isAbsolute(path);\n}\n\nexport function taskFiles(task) {\n  if (!task || !/^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$/.test(task)) throw new Error('Supply a task ID from rehearsal/prompts.');\n  return {\n    prompt: join(rehearsal, 'prompts', task + '.md'),\n    fixture: join(rehearsal, 'fixtures', task + '.json'),\n    expected: join(rehearsal, 'fixtures', task + '.expected.json'),\n  };\n}\n\nexport async function readJson(file) {\n  return JSON.parse(await readFile(file, 'utf8'));\n}\n\nexport async function writeJson(file, value) {\n  const temporary = file + '.' + randomUUID() + '.tmp';\n  try {\n    await writeFile(temporary, JSON.stringify(value, null, 2) + '\\n', { flag: 'wx' });\n    await rename(temporary, file);\n  } finally {\n    await rm(temporary, { force: true });\n  }\n}\n\nexport function isMain(url) {\n  return !!process.argv[1] && pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href === url;\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
